**In a hurry?** Jump to [the complete file](#the-complete-file), copy it, and change the values called out under **For your robot**. The numbered parts explain each piece in a sentence or two. You do not need to understand all of it to get moving: the pages under **Understanding** go deeper when you want them.
{% endhint %}

## 1. Describe the arm

`ArmConfig` describes the arm itself: its length and its hard limits. The simulation uses both. The hard limits are where the arm physically stops, which is different from the soft limits you set in step 1.

<figure><img src="https://1354553280-files.gitbook.io/~/files/v0/b/gitbook-x-prod.appspot.com/o/spaces%2FZM0CFmYiQzcrY4zDcTtZ%2Fuploads%2Fgit-blob-309f8e0214d8774fbbf0a818888126af56d043bd%2Ftutorial-arm-angles.png?alt=media" alt="A side view of the arm and the angles used in this tutorial. The hard limits are minus 30 and 40 degrees: where the arm physically stops, set on ArmConfig and used by the simulation. The soft limits are minus 20 and 30 degrees: as far as the closed loop will go, set on SmartMotorControllerConfig. Inside them are the setpoints: minus 5 degrees for the A button, which is also where the arm starts, 15 degrees for the B button, and 0 degrees for the default command."><figcaption><p>The soft limits from step 1 sit inside the hard limits from this step.</p></figcaption></figure>

