## 3. Bind the buttons

`whileTrue` runs a command for as long as its button is held, and cancels it on release. The default command then takes back over.

<figure><img src="https://1354553280-files.gitbook.io/~/files/v0/b/gitbook-x-prod.appspot.com/o/spaces%2FZM0CFmYiQzcrY4zDcTtZ%2Fuploads%2Fgit-blob-7d1a6f53a140fb87c1a17a2cd90bb5582a98e559%2Ftutorial-arm-buttons.gif?alt=media" alt="Animation of the four face buttons of a controller, the arm, and the command that is running. With no button held the default command runs: hold the arm at 0 degrees. While A is held its command runs: hold the arm at minus 5 degrees. While B is held: hold the arm at 15 degrees. While X is held the arm is driven at a 30 percent duty cycle with the closed loop off. Each time a button is released the default command takes back over."><figcaption><p>A held button owns the arm. Let go, and the default command brings it back to 0°.</p></figcaption></figure>

