## 7. Starting position and soft limits

The starting position is where the elevator is when the robot turns on. The soft limits are as far as the closed loop is allowed to take it.

<figure><img src="https://1354553280-files.gitbook.io/~/files/v0/b/gitbook-x-prod.appspot.com/o/spaces%2FZM0CFmYiQzcrY4zDcTtZ%2Fuploads%2Fgit-blob-b4934b97bacb73e6df57d1dc94e5c782997037e8%2Fsmc-soft-limits.png?alt=media" alt="A bar showing a mechanism&#x27;s travel between two hard stops, with a lower and an upper soft limit a little inside them. The mechanism may move between the soft limits. A setpoint asked for beyond the upper limit is moved back to the limit."><figcaption><p>Soft limits sit a little inside the hard stops.</p></figcaption></figure>

{% tabs %}
{% tab title="Java, Commands v2" %}
{% code title="subsystems/ElevatorSubsystem.java" %}

```java
