## 1. Describe the elevator

`ElevatorConfig` describes the elevator itself: its hard limits and the weight of its carriage. The simulation uses both. The hard limits are where the carriage physically stops, which is different from the soft limits you set in step 1.

<figure><img src="https://1354553280-files.gitbook.io/~/files/v0/b/gitbook-x-prod.appspot.com/o/spaces%2FZM0CFmYiQzcrY4zDcTtZ%2Fuploads%2Fgit-blob-3cf96dd36e04b25ad3da7b5d3a40e3730be81724%2Ftutorial-elevator-heights.png?alt=media" alt="A side view of the elevator and the heights used in this tutorial. The hard limits are 0 and 3 meters: where the carriage physically stops, set on ElevatorConfig and used by the simulation. The soft limits are 0 and 2 meters: as far as the closed loop will go, set on SmartMotorControllerConfig. Inside them are the setpoints: 0.5 meters for the A button, 1 meter for the B button, and 0 meters for the default command, which is also where the carriage starts."><figcaption><p>The soft limits from step 1 sit inside the hard limits from this step.</p></figcaption></figure>

