## 3. Bind the buttons

`whileTrue` runs a command for as long as its button is held, and cancels it on release. The default command then takes back over.

<figure><img src="https://1354553280-files.gitbook.io/~/files/v0/b/gitbook-x-prod.appspot.com/o/spaces%2FZM0CFmYiQzcrY4zDcTtZ%2Fuploads%2Fgit-blob-0fc5e90d8bfb48b6d8993524dec3f62a7fb75d70%2Ftutorial-shooter-buttons.gif?alt=media" alt="Animation of the four face buttons of a controller, the flywheel, and the command that is running. With no button held the default command runs: a duty cycle of 0, so the flywheel coasts. While A is held its command runs: hold the flywheel at 60 RPM. While B is held: hold the flywheel at 300 RPM. While X is held the flywheel is driven at a 30 percent duty cycle with the closed loop off. Each time a button is released the default command takes back over."><figcaption><p>A held button owns the flywheel. Let go, and the default command lets it coast down.</p></figcaption></figure>

