## 1. Read the sticks, and drive with them

A `SwerveInputStream` turns the raw stick values into field relative chassis speeds, with the deadband, the cubing and the alliance flip already applied. A drive command gives those speeds to the drive every loop.

<figure><img src="https://1354553280-files.gitbook.io/~/files/v0/b/gitbook-x-prod.appspot.com/o/spaces%2FZM0CFmYiQzcrY4zDcTtZ%2Fuploads%2Fgit-blob-3ee61c10559baa352ec85e34e455187fc161cfd6%2Fswerve-input-stream-sticks.gif?alt=media" alt="Animation of two controller sticks, the ChassisVelocities they produce, and a robot on a field. Left stick forward gives positive vx and the robot moves away from the driver station. Left stick left gives positive vy and the robot moves left. A diagonal push gives both. Right stick left gives a positive omega and the robot turns counter-clockwise"><figcaption><p>How each stick movement becomes a field relative velocity.</p></figcaption></figure>

