{% hint style="warning" %}
**LQR Controller Execution**: LQR is **not natively supported** by any motor controller hardware. When configured, the closed loop control runs on the **SystemCore**: the wrapper starts a `Notifier` that calls `SmartMotorController.iterateClosedLoopController()` every closed loop control period (20 ms unless you set `withClosedLoopControlPeriod`), so there is nothing to call yourself. See [LQR Controllers](/documentation/understanding/editor/lqr-controllers.md) for details.
{% endhint %}

{% hint style="info" %}
**Nova Closed Loop Execution**: `NovaWrapper` always runs its closed loop controller (PID or [LQR](/documentation/understanding/editor/lqr-controllers.md), motion profiles and feedforwards) on the SystemCore and commands the Nova with voltage. ThriftyLib's simulation ignores the Nova's onboard PID gains, so this keeps simulation and the real robot the same. A YAMS alert reports that the closed loop controller is running on the SystemCore.
{% endhint %}

