| Follower Inversion        | ✅       | ✅        | ✅             | ✅    |
| Loosely Coupled Followers | ✅       | ✅        | ✅             | ✅    |

{% hint style="warning" %}
**Follower Compatibility**: Followers must be the same brand as the leader motor controller. You cannot mix vendors for hardware followers. Within a vendor the models can be mixed: a TalonFX can follow a TalonFXS and a TalonFXS can follow a TalonFX, and a SPARK MAX and a SPARK Flex can follow each other. Loosely coupled followers are different: each one runs its own closed loop, so you can mix brands freely, such as a SPARK leading a TalonFX.
{% endhint %}

### Telemetry

| Feature                 | TalonFX | TalonFXS | SparkMax/Flex | Nova |
| ----------------------- | ------- | -------- | ------------- | ---- |
| Telemetry Name          | ✅       | ✅        | ✅             | ✅    |
| Telemetry Verbosity     | ✅       | ✅        | ✅             | ✅    |
| Custom Telemetry Config | ✅       | ✅        | ✅             | ✅    |

### Simulation

| Feature              | TalonFX | TalonFXS | SparkMax/Flex | Nova |
| -------------------- | ------- | -------- | ------------- | ---- |
| DCMotorSim           | ✅       | ✅        | ✅             | ✅    |
| Moment of Inertia    | ✅       | ✅        | ✅             | ✅    |
| Custom Sim Supplier  | ✅       | ✅        | ✅             | ✅    |
| External Encoder Sim | ✅       | ✅        | ✅             | ✅    |

### Safety features

| Feature            | TalonFX                                                                                   | TalonFXS                                                                                  | SparkMax/Flex                                                                                                    | Nova                           |
| ------------------ | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------ |
| Temperature Cutoff | ⚠️ (requires an [LQR controller](/documentation/understanding/editor/lqr-controllers.md)) | ⚠️ (requires an [LQR controller](/documentation/understanding/editor/lqr-controllers.md)) | ⚠️ (requires an exponential profile or [LQR controller](/documentation/understanding/editor/lqr-controllers.md)) | ⚠️ (requires closed loop mode) |

{% hint style="warning" %}
**Temperature Cutoff**: the cutoff is checked by the closed loop running on the SystemCore, so it only works where the loop runs there. That is an [LQR controller](/documentation/understanding/editor/lqr-controllers.md) on any motor controller, an Exponential Profile on a `SparkWrapper`, and always on a `NovaWrapper`. With PID or a profile that runs on the motor controller, it does not work.
{% endhint %}

